      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "> U N I T Y    P R E S E T S\n\nBut yes, would be cool to have some optimization in the options...how could the devs do it though when the issues arise from worlds and avatars? \n\nAll I can think of is make some non-editable clause in the SDK to prevent avatars over a certain poly count to be able to load on the 'optimized' client. Or replace it with a default one like UnityChan. (Non-editable to prevent crash avatars filtering through with modified SDKs)",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
